Track 1: "Mother May I Cut The Power?"
- Story & Context: On a freezing November dusk at Junction 9 Overpass, Marcus Vance jammed a modified auxiliary cable into the regional arterial junction box, short-circuiting twenty-two miles of commuter traffic into a standstill as the smell of scorched ozone and burnt road-grit blanketed the highway. When the automated emergency klaxons began their mechanical wail, the crew seized the public address speakers, dropping a punishing 195-BPM kick-drill pattern that shook the structural girders until the stranded truck drivers climbed out not to fight, but to watch. "Hold the curb, kill the green, tell the state we are unseen," Tariq barked into a modified CB microphone, crystallizing the riot that birthed the entire sound.
