Track 2: Pavements Forfeit Four-Square
- Story & Context: Huddled inside a disused toll booth at the Lower Quay Underpass, municipal surveillance technician Sora Lin watched lukewarm filter coffee drip across her log sheets as she secretly routed the city’s pedestrian-crossing acoustic beacons into the syndicate's master clap bus. Her taped confession—admitting she had sabotaged the curfew warning alarms because her younger brother had been arrested during the cloverleaf sweeps—became the tragic emotional spine of the track. Above a lurching half-time drill bounce and hammering iron claps, her voice wavered against Tariq's spitfire delivery: "Count to four before you bleed, step inside the square we freed."
